<title>CANADA: CWB details Prairie elevator space, railcar unload.</title>
<headline>CWB details Prairie elevator space, railcar unload.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vacant space in Canadian Prairie primary elevators increased to 27 percent in the week ended May 18 while railcar unloads totalled 82 percent of their targetted levels, Canadian Wheat Board said.</p>
<p>The average vacancy in Prairie elevators was 27 perc4 percent on May 11.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan had the least space available at 25 percent, Manitoba was next at 26 percent and Alberta had the most vacant space at 29 percent.</p>
<p>Vancouver unloaded 2,636 railcars versus the 3,300 target. Prince Rupert unloaded 700 railcars versus the 1,300 target.</p>
<p>Thunder Bay unloads totalled 2,961 versus the 3,075 target.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
